  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1137 PM CDT Mon Jul 13 2026\n\nAs we move into the late week and into the weekend, ample moisture \nwill still be in place with the upper high to our north and east. \nThis will help temperatures climb closer to the mid 80s to lower 90s \nalong with dew points in the low to mid 70s. Heat index values will \nclimb closer to 100 degrees. Model guidance has increased daily PoPs \nThursday through Saturday from low to low to medium. This is due to \nmodels picking up on the potential for a couple of shortwaves moving \nfrom SE to NW across the area. By Sunday or Monday, the very deep \nmoisture looks like it will get swept east of the area which should \nhelp bring down PoPs.",
